{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140355-question-about-worms-and-giants","id":1140355,"title":"Question about \"Worms and Giants\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-14T16:51:37-07:00","id":1140355,"title":"Question about \"Worms and Giants\"","content":"Question for the more experienced, as I'm very new to Changeling and just getting started at learning about how Arts and Realms work:<br /> <br /> How do you handle uses of Worms and Giants? For example, the book talks about turning table knives into impromptu swords... but after expanding a knife to sword-size, the handle would probably be quite large and difficult to grip. Do you allow the object to grow slightly out of proportion to accommodate the desires of the fae affecting it? Or do you describe the grip as unpleasant or possibly even give a penalty?<br /> <br /> As an offshoot of that question, what about shrinking or expanding parts of a more complicated item? Changing a single pin or spring in a firearm, or altering a bore's diameter could make it useless or possibly even dangerous to wield. Using Prop and Scene, could a Changeling affect all the bullets in a room (-just- the bullets, not the bullet cartridges)... shrinking them down so they fall out of their cartridges and making every firearm in range useless?<br /> <br /> It strikes me this power has a ton of utility... almost frighteningly so... unless there's more to it I'm not picking up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T18:01:43-07:00","id":1140938,"title":"","content":"Since I haven't gotten any replies, allow me to rephrase the question:<br /> <br /> How do/would you run it in your games and at your table, regarding the above types of scenarios? If you're running a game, would you allow a restaurant steak knife to be transformed into a sword or machete, ready to go with normal stats? Would you let your PC disable a firearm by messing with one of its components, or partially dismantle ammunition in a room by shrinking the projectiles from out of their casings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T21:57:50-07:00","id":1140983,"title":"","content":"It's hard questions you've asked. Let's see. <br /> <br /> What is good about C20 is that Unleashing allows to cover for Cantrips' limitations. So, I'd say:<br /> 1. Attack penalty on a over-sized knife, depending on the form of the handle and bulkiness of the Blade (but not less, than +2 difficulty). Some knifes are more likely cause blunt damage, than lethal, some you shouldn't even bother with. Trolls probably may negate some of the penalty, due to their sheer size and opppsite for small-ish Kith. If difficulty raises to 9 or more, don't bother with it as a weapon and consider throwing it, given you have enough Steength. If it's chimerical knife or dagger, that changed, I'd say it should be much more easy to handle.<br /> 2. Changing parts of gun seems, like a stretch to me, but you could always Unleash for that. Better to shrink the whole gun, bullets and all.<br /> 3. Prop and Scene, with enough Glamour to feed it plus the whatever the Difficulty you're up against to shrink bullets. Dunno. Maybe with Props, required to affect guns +1 as a justification, than probably, yes. <br /> <br /> Now I think it would be fun to have a Realm of Exposition for everything else, that isn't explicitly covered by existing Realms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}